            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of hypertensive emergencies in the elderly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-9, 83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although the diminishing number of hypertensive emergencies is gratifying, it is nevertheless unfortunate that a significant proportion of hypertensive patients of all ages still are not receiving effective long-term treatment. Hypertensive emergencies continue to threaten many patients. Early recognition and aggressive management provide the best means to reduce morbidity and mortality in many hypertensive emergencies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
